course: dictionary
lesson: 8756
title: One word, many meanings: setup
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Setup has several, so the sentence around it tells you which one to pick. Look at the clues: the words near it are its context.
explain: «Setup blocks belong at the top of a script; at the bottom they only run after everything else.» Here setup means the start, the part that gets things ready before the rest runs. Top and script are the clues.
explain: «Setup blocks, like "go to x: 0 y: 0", belong at the top, so the sprite starts in the same place every time.» The clue is "so the sprite starts in the same place every time": setup blocks prepare the sprite before the program begins.
explain: Always try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one. A dictionary settles it when the clues are not enough.
fact: Setup as a noun can mean the way things are arranged, like a gaming setup or a classroom setup.
fact: Setup can also mean getting something ready to use, like a setup wizard on a new phone.
fact: Informally, «It's a setup!» means someone has been tricked on purpose to look guilty or foolish.
fact: In a story or joke, the setup is the first part that introduces the characters and the place before the problem appears.
fact: As a verb it is two words, «set up», and its forms are «sets up», «set up» and «setting up».
exercise: Which sentence uses setup as a noun? | They set up the tent by the river. | *Her gaming setup is amazing. | He sets up the chairs every morning. | She will set up the printer after lunch.
exercise: In «Setup blocks belong at the top of a script», what does setup mean? | *The start, which gets things ready before the rest runs | A broken computer that will not turn on | A trick planned to fool someone | The final part of a story
exercise: «It was a setup!» shouts the detective. What does setup mean here? | A way of arranging a classroom | A long and happy holiday | *A trick planned to make someone look guilty | A new computer being switched on
test: In a story, what is the setup? | The happy ending at the very end | The problem that the hero has to solve | *The beginning that introduces the characters and place before the problem | A type of computer file
test: What does a setup wizard help you do on a new phone? | *Get the phone ready to use | Play a game with your friends | Turn the phone into a tablet | Plan a trick for someone
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Put the setup blocks at the top, so the sprite starts in the right place»? | A bad mood after a long day | A trick planned to fool someone | *The instructions that get things ready at the start | The bottom part of a script
